<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6889" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carsĕŏli</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καρσέολοι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of the Æqui</i>, <i>in Latium</i>, now the village <i>Carsoli</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 10, 3, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 13, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 27, 9</span></i>; 10, 29,
			15; <i><span class="en">Vell.
				1, 14, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 4, 683</span></i>.— Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carsĕŏlānus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of Carseoli</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 9, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					4, 710</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carsĕŏlāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Carseoli</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 12,
				17, § 106</span></i>.—And in <i>neutr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in Carseolano,</span>”
				<i>in the region of Carseoli</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 23, 35, § 213</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
